# The preview iframe is sandboxed WITHOUT allow-same-origin, so student code
# cannot call /api/* as the student. That makes it an OPAQUE origin, and an
# opaque origin's fetches are cross-origin with `Origin: null`.
#
# A classic <script src> is fetched no-cors, which is why the JSCAD bundle loads
# there today without any of this. An ES MODULE is always fetched in CORS mode,
# and so is the .wasm an emscripten module pulls in -- so a module-shipped
# kernel is blocked before its wasm is even requested. Measured 2026-09-01:
# without this header the OpenCascade build fails at the module script with
# "from origin 'null' has been blocked by CORS policy"; with it, the kernel
# initialises inside the real sandbox with all 498 exports live.
#
# Safe because these are already public static assets -- allowing a cross-origin
# READ of a file anyone can request changes nothing. It deliberately does NOT
# cover /api/*, which stays same-origin and cookie-gated.
/reshape/kernel/*
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: cross-origin
